{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794173752,"nonce":"ab2fRSfnAQ1Q+aCW++rZ6Z6weto=","message":"Built as approved, with these additions (none changes a decision):\n\n- An override of the built-in `color` (`fields: {color: {name: ...}}`) is refused by `schema import` on a type whose entry lacks `color: true`, naming the fix; a stored override on a type that has since switched color off is kept in the store and compiled as nothing (lenient on read).\n- `color` is written as the type attribute `color` (owned by the import, so an import of the type without `color: true` removes it, as `retype_targets` is removed).\n- The palette for uncoloured gantt groups indexes by each group's place among all groups (a coloured head's place counts), so setting one head's colour recolours no other group and, with no colour anywhere, every group keeps today's colour. Recorded under views.md \"Gantt groups are colors\" with its Not-X.\n- The creator page and ghosts drop a drafted `color` on a retype to a type without it, as any foreign field is dropped (`schema.OnEveryType`).\n- `git work quickstart`'s live section says which types carry `color`.\n- doc/design/issue.md \"The built-in fields\" names the fifth built-in.","files":null}]}